## 2. Summary of Fixes (F1 – F7)

### **F1 — Single Validated Row-Stream Layer (`LegacySource`)**
- **Architecture**: Implemented [`LegacySource`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp2/libs/migrate/src/migrate/legacy_source.py) yielding standard immutable units (`FlatFactUnit`, `BatchUnit`, `TickUnit`).
- **Consolidation**: Both [`inventory()`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp2/libs/migrate/src/migrate/inventory.py) and [`transform()`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp2/libs/migrate/src/migrate/transform.py) now consume `LegacySource.read(source)`. Duplicated parsing, batch-envelope iteration, and validation loops in `inventory.py` and `transform.py` were completely removed.
- **SQLite Semantic Validation**: The SQLite arm applies full semantic row-level validation (finite numeric `ts`, string types on `id`/`kind`/`origin`/`payload`/`signature`, non-empty `observer`) before yielding.
- **Seam Defense**: All 3 seam defense tests (`mixed-observer`, `absent-observer`, `codec-invalid`) were mirrored onto the SQLite arm and assert typed `LegacySourceRefused` (never `ArrivalBodyError`, `JsonlCodecError`, `KeyError`, or `TypeError`).
- **Ruled Ordering**: The SQLite facts-then-ticks ruled ordering is documented in the [`LegacySource`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp2/libs/migrate/src/migrate/legacy_source.py) docstring.

### **F2 — Empty-Observer Cohort (`observer=''`)**
- **Classification**: `observer=''` joins the absent class across JSONL and SQLite arms (batches, flat facts, ticks).
- **Spelling Distinction**: Both structured data and formatted messages preserve the exact spelling count (`empty` vs `missing`): e.g. `line 2: 1 row(s) with observer='' (empty string)`.
- **Pre-target Bytes**: Refusal fires at `inventory()` before any arrival draft bytes or sidecar transforms are attempted.
- **G.3 Cleanup**: Removed `if fr.observer:` guards from §G.3 census reporting since empty observer is refused upstream.

### **F3 — Dropping-Rule Regroup Discipline (Refuse-Not-Split)**
- **Partial Batch Drop**: If `map_fact` returns `None` for some but not all rows of a batch group, [`transform()`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp2/libs/migrate/src/migrate/transform.py) raises typed [`BatchRegroupRefused`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp2/libs/migrate/src/migrate/refusals.py) (subclass of `MigrationRefused`). Deleted batch→fact collapse and kind re-deciding logic.
- **Whole-Unit Drop**: If `map_fact` drops all rows of a batch or a flat fact, the whole-unit drop is recorded in [`TransformExceptions.dropped_units`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp2/libs/migrate/src/migrate/transform.py) as [`DroppedUnit(coordinate, kind, rule)`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp2/libs/migrate/src/migrate/transform.py) and emits no draft.

### **F4 — Required `signer` Parameter**
- **Enforcement**: [`transform()`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp2/libs/migrate/src/migrate/transform.py) signature narrowed to `signer: Signer` (required keyword-only argument, no default). Omitting `signer` raises `TypeError` at the call site.
- **No Unsigned Path**: Key introductions are strictly signed via `signer`; no code path constructs an unsigned key introduction draft.

### **F5 — Declared-Key Shape Validation**
- **Shape Validation**: Validates all declared observer public keys (and custodian key) at transform setup using `_key_shape_fault` imported from `engine.arrival`.
- **Typed Refusal**: Malformed declared keys raise typed [`DeclarationKeyRefused`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp2/libs/migrate/src/migrate/refusals.py) naming the offending observer.

### **F6 — Residue & Typing Sweep**
- **Dead Imports**: Removed unused imports (`_KEY_INTRODUCTION_KIND`, `_content_sha256`, `_facts_have_signature`, `_tick_columns`, etc.) across `inventory.py` and `transform.py`.
- **Vertex Narrowing**: Parameter `vertex` in `transform()` narrowed to `VertexFile`. Added [`coerce_vertex(vertex: VertexFile | Path | str) -> VertexFile`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp2/libs/migrate/src/migrate/transform.py#L125) helper.
- **Format Inspection**: Removed `.jsonl` / `.sqlite` file extension branching from `transform()`; format inspection is governed by magic header detection inside `LegacySource`.
- **Custodian Key Refusal**: Missing custodian public key in `.vertex` raises typed [`MissingCustodianKeyRefused`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp2/libs/migrate/src/migrate/refusals.py) (subclass of `MigrationRefused`).

### **F7 — Test-Strength Gaps**
- **F7a**: Added [`test_intra_batch_row_order_preserved`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp2/libs/migrate/tests/test_transform.py#L448) to assert exact source sequence retention in emitted batch drafts.
- **F7b**: Added authored signature `"sig-alice-batch-2"` to `BATCH_ROW_2` in [`tests/_fixtures.py`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp2/libs/migrate/tests/_fixtures.py#L74) and asserted verbatim signature preservation in `test_signature_byte_preservation_and_honest_absence`.

